        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T08:02:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): the Face raster takes a start pick and an exit pick\n\nThe Face always started its raster at the corner that the generator\nselected. The start pick now takes the corner of the face region nearest\nto it: its edge row is cut first and the rows step to the far edge. The\nexit pick names the side where the last row ends. A side that the row\ncount cannot reach from the start corner is refused by name. An exit pick\nalone chooses the start corner that reaches it.\n\nThe rows never change: a pick only orders the facer's own band, so the\noverrun, the holes law, the \"Do not touch\" law and the air entry read the\nsame rows. No pick is the automatic raster to the byte.\n\n- motion: `face_raster` (the planning rule) and `face_picked` (the entry\n  point); `face_over_kept` calls it with no pick.\n- app: Face answers `PickCapability::Raster`; the picks are turned into\n  the laid frame of an open boundary; a tilted (3+2) Face refuses a pick\n  by name.\n- mcp: the `edit_operation` schema names the Face rule.\n- ui: the Face Geometry tab shows typed Start point and Exit point groups.\n\nFixes #3326\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
