      "message": "fix(2d): the Face picks hold under a rotated work offset and a keep-out\n\nReview of PR #3997, findings 1 and 2.\n\n- A work offset with a Z rotation carries the geometry into the\n  generator frame. `wcs_yaw::rotate_params` now carries each start and\n  exit pick with it (`OpParams::path_picks_mut`, each kind that stores\n  picks). The Face read the picks in the setup's frame against a rotated\n  region, so the model pick (29, 19) took the wrong corner.\n- The picks are judged again on the rows that each level cuts\n  (`face_raster::Raster::held`). A hole or a \"Do not touch\" keep-out that\n  takes the first or the last row is refused with the blocked pick named\n  and marked. Before, the exit was accepted from the uncut row count and\n  the cut ended on the other side.\n\nPinned by `a_rotated_work_offset_reads_the_picks_in_the_setup_frame`\n(app) and\n`a_keep_out_that_takes_a_terminal_row_refuses_the_blocked_pick_by_name`\n(motion).\n\nRefs #3326\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
